# The build context for every service whose `context:` is the repository root --
# today `harness` and `web`.
#
# THE FIRST ENTRY IS A PRIVATE KEY AND IT IS THE REASON THIS FILE EXISTS.
# swap_terminal/grc-sol-swap/abstergo_exchange/wgrc.json is an ed25519 Solana
# keypair, present on disk and untracked. The abstergo image already excluded it
# through that directory's own .dockerignore -- and then `harness` and `web` were
# added with `context: .`, which reintroduced the identical hazard from a
# completely different direction, because a .dockerignore applies to ONE context
# and the root is a different context.
#
# Measured 2026-10-05 before this file existed: the root tree is 82M, of which
# .git is 46M, and the keypair was inside it. `docker build` uploads the ENTIRE
# context to the daemon before the first instruction runs, so two builds a day
# meant two copies of a private key into a build cache that nothing in this
# repository can see or clean. No COPY line ever referenced it; that was never
# the hazard.
#
# Its value has not been read.
swap_terminal/grc-sol-swap/abstergo_exchange/wgrc.json
# Belt and braces: any keypair-shaped name anywhere, because the lesson of
# 2026-09-25 is that `*keypair*.json` in .gitignore did not match a file called
# wgrc.json. A name pattern is a guess about what somebody names a secret, so the
# explicit path above is the real guard and these are only the obvious cases.
**/*keypair*.json
**/id.json
.env
**/.env

# NOTHING THAT BUILDS NEEDS THE HISTORY. 46M of the 82M.
.git
.gitignore

# The whole abstergo subtree. It has its OWN image with its OWN context, and
# neither harness nor web COPYs anything from it -- including services/gridcoin.js,
# whose POST /deposit route sends Gridcoin with no authentication at all
# (auth.js:37).
swap_terminal/grc-sol-swap

# THE VIRTUALENV, AND IT WAS NOT HERE UNTIL 2026-10-05. Measured on the
# operator's host: `docker build` for the web service transferred 58.70MB of
# context, against 82M of tree with .git (46M) already excluded -- the difference
# is almost entirely .venv, which this file did not name. It is tens of megabytes
# of somebody else's compiled wheels, uploaded to the daemon on every build, and
# the image installs its own from requirements.txt so none of it is even used.
#
# pyproject.toml's ruff `exclude` has listed .venv since the file existed, so the
# repository already knew the name. This file simply did not ask it.
.venv
venv
env
.tox
*.egg-info

# Caches and build output. __pycache__ in particular would ship .pyc files
# compiled by whatever interpreter last ran here, next to the .py the image
# installs -- and a stale .pyc beside a newer .py is a file that runs and is not
# the file you are reading.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.log
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
**/node_modules

# Not needed by either image. The web image deliberately ships no root tools and
# no tests (see its Dockerfile), and docs are 0 bytes of runtime behavior.
tests
docs
assets
requirements-dev.txt
# 5.49MB measured, and no Dockerfile COPYs a single file from it. tools/warbot and
# tools/dleq_helper are operator-side helpers; the dleq_helper is a compiled binary
# whose own .gitignore entry says its failure mode is "the cryptography is wrong".
tools

# RUNTIME STATE, AND THIS ONE IS NOT TIDINESS. It holds the container volume mount
# points AND, under swap_terminal/, the live worker pid files, worker logs and
# kill_switch.lock. A swap_intents.json or a pid file baked into an image SHADOWS
# the volume mounted over it in exactly the cases where the mount fails -- so the
# image would quietly serve a snapshot of whenever somebody last built, for files
# that decide whether funds are released and whether a stop can be proven.
#
# `**/runtime` AND NOT `runtime`, AND THAT WAS A REAL BUG UNTIL 2026-10-05.
# .dockerignore patterns are matched against the path relative to the CONTEXT
# ROOT, so a bare `runtime` excluded ./runtime and nothing else --
# swap_terminal/runtime/ went in every time, pid files and all. Measured on the
# operator's host: the web build transferred 60.27MB of context AFTER .venv was
# excluded, and that directory holds the logs of workers at cycle=3507 and
# cycle=5344.
#
# The same root-anchoring applies to `*.log` below, which was excluding exactly
# zero files because every log in this tree is at least one directory deep.
**/runtime

# Databases never belong in an image. swap_terminal.db is mounted, and a copy in
# the image would be a second source of truth with no reconciliation -- the thing
# CLAUDE.md rule 15 is entirely about.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite3

docker-compose.yml
